-- title:
--   Ideal sheaf of a closed point generated by a uniformiser
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be an integral scheme and $K$ a field, and let $j \colon \operatorname{Spec} K \to X$ be a closed immersion; write $P = j(\mathfrak{m})$ for the image under $j$ of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} K$. Let $W$ be an open subset of $X$ with $P \in W$, and let $a \in \Gamma(X, W)$ be a section subject to four hypotheses: its image under the map $\Gamma(X,W) \to \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} K, j^{-1}W)$ induced by $j$ is $0$; the germ of $a$ at $P$ generates the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X,P}$; for every $z \in W$ with $z \neq P$ the germ of $a$ at $z$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$; and $W$ contains at least one point different from $P$. The conclusion is that for every affine open $U$ of $X$ with $U \leq W$, writing $a|_U \in \Gamma(X,U)$ for the restriction of $a$, the ideal cut out on $U$ by the kernel ideal sheaf $\ker j$ of $j$ equals the principal ideal generated by $a|_U$, and $a|_U$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\Gamma(X,U)$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a section vanishing to first order at a rational point $P$ and invertible elsewhere generates the ideal sheaf of $P$ over any affine open, together with the assertion that such a generator is a non-zero-divisor, so that the ideal sheaf is an invertible module. It is applied, on models of modular curves, to identify ideal modules of sections with explicit line bundles, in both [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.nonempty_pullback_baseChangeSnd_iso_ofPoint_tensor_idealModule_of_isFrameOn_of_map_eq_smul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.nonempty_pullback_baseChangeSnd_iso_ofPoint_tensor_idealModule_of_isFrameOn_of_map_eq_smul) and [`ModularCurve.XOneP.nonempty_pullback_iso_ofPoint_tensor_idealModule_of_isFrameOn_of_map_eq_smul_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.nonempty_pullback_iso_ofPoint_tensor_idealModule_of_isFrameOn_of_map_eq_smul_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
